# Unconditional holomorphic blowdown descent

For the actual incidence blowup, every actual holomorphic scalar
function descends uniquely along its projection to an entire function
on the affine plane. The two-chart corollary uses only entire chart
functions and their actual blowup overlap identity.

The proof uses compact-complex constancy on the exceptional sphere,
proper quotient descent, the actual punctured biholomorphism, and
continuous removability on one-variable coordinate slices. No
normality, rationality, direct-image, or acyclicity assumption occurs.
-/
